                <pb facs="0394" n="296" sameAs="frus:frus1900/pg296"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum handed to the Secretary by the Chinese
                        Minister.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Chinese Legation</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1900-10-02"><hi rendition="#italic">October 2,
                        1900</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>A cablegram received from Director-General Sheng, at Shanghai, states that by an
                    Imperial edict issued on September 25 Prince Chwang, Prince Yi, Secondary
                    Princes Tsai Lien and Tsai Ying are deprived of all their respective ranks and
                    offices; that Prince Tuan (as an act of clemency) is deprived of office and is
                    handed over to the Imperial clan court, which shall consult and decide upon a
                    severe penalty, and his salary is to be stopped; that Duke Tsai Lan and the
                    president of the censorate Ying Nien are handed over to the said board, who
                    shall consult and decide upon a severe penalty, and that Kang Yi, assistant
                    grand secretary and president of the civil board, and Chao-Shu-Chiao, president
                    of the board of punishments, are handed over to the board of censors, who shall
                    consult and decide upon a penalty.</p>
